grAlphaControlsITRGBLighting: texel alpha picks the colour combine's local colour

grAlphaControlsITRGBLighting( FXTRUE ) turns on the Voodoo's alpha-controlled lighting (SST-1
fbzColorPath cc_localselect_override): the top bit of each texel's alpha then picks the colour
combine's local colour, the iterated (vertex) colour when it is clear and the constant colour when
it is set, whatever grColorCombine's local says. OpenGLide had the entry point as an empty stub,
so the local colour was always the combine's own (the iterated colour, as a 1998 game sets it).
That game draws its textures, mostly grey with colour in places, times the local colour, and keeps
its team colour (green) in the vertex colours: the texels meant to show their own colour under the
constant (white or grey) light came out in the team colour too, and its vehicles, their pads and
its vehicle hangar were monochrome green.

- The state is kept (GlideState.AlphaControlsITRGB, saved and restored by grGlideGetState and
  grGlideSetState; grSstWinOpen already turns it off), and setting it draws the triangles queued
  before.
- RenderAddTriangle() computes each corner's colour twice while it is on: with the iterated
  colour as local, as before, and with the constant colour as local (TColorAlt).
- RenderDrawTriangles(), for a texture the vertex colour modulates (GL_MODULATE: the texture
  environment of most colour combines), sets texture unit 0 to INTERPOLATE(constant, vertex
  colour, texture alpha), with the second colour as the environment's constant, set per run of
  triangles that share it, and unit 1, with the same texture, to multiply that by the texture's
  colour; the alpha stays texture alpha times vertex alpha. The draw itself moves into
  RenderDrawRange() and RenderDrawRangeChroma() (the chroma-key path), which draw a range of the
  queued triangles, unchanged otherwise.
- Not covered: the hardware picks by the top bit, here a texel with an alpha in between gets a
  mix of the two colours; the colour of a triangle's first corner stands for the whole triangle
  (it varies over a triangle only when the combine's other or factor is iterated too); the decal
  and blend environments, a texture split over two units (AP_88), lines and points.

For wsh-pve (packages/wsh-openglide), against kjliew/qemu-xtra at the commit upstream.env pins,
after 0003-egl-dmabuf-scanout.patch.
